The ACL MAC patch is carried by explicit release-owner decision in #175.
Its 0002 prefix reserves 0001 for the independently reviewed NTP proposal
in #164; it does not enable or approve that proposal (#129).

If #164 is approved, preserve every carried patch file and every series entry
when resolving its add/add series conflict. Never choose one side wholesale.
Run the patch-series application checks and the sonic-utilities ACL/NTP tests
against the resulting series and the pinned sonic-utilities source.

0003 exposes APPL_DB remote-VNI requests without a matching same-namespace
STATE_DB tunnel entry (issue #187, partial observability follow-up to #73).
It preserves existing operational-state rows and count semantics, and does
not infer ASIC state or a capacity/failure diagnosis from missing tunnel state.
The carried CLI tests cover multiple VNIs, IPv6, namespace isolation and
empty/deleted/partial records. Keep it alongside the ACL patch and any
independently approved NTP patch when resolving series conflicts.

0005 makes the ports that 'config interface breakout' creates inherit mtu
and fec from the ports they replace, as decided on #197: the highest mtu of
the old ports, and the fec of the first old port in lane order whose fec is
set and not 'none'. Without an active fec, a new port keeps the fec that
platform.json gives it (rs for 50G+ per lane) or gets 'none'; without an mtu
on any old port, no mtu is written. admin_status, description,
dhcp_rate_limit and SFLOW_SESSION are not inherited (follow-ups on #197).
The patch is independent of 0004 (#136); keep both when resolving series
conflicts.
